 "data_checks": {
  "reserve_offset": "On sells, sol = R_s*tok/(R_t+tok) holds with R_s = pool_sol_logged + 17.585 (train sample of 94,624 sells: p90 = p99 = 17.5845). The true reserve is logged PLUS ~17.6, not minus. Main runs use +17.585; the brief's -17.6 estimate is a coded sensitivity (only run for configs that pass, none did; it only increases impact).",
  "fee_bps": "fee_bps already sums lp + protocol + creator bps (pipeline/market.py load_amm); on sells user_sol/sol = 1 - fee_bps/1e4 (median 0.988 at fee_bps 120). Main runs charge fee_bps/1e4 per side; the brief's extra 0.25% would be double counting and is a sensitivity only.",
  "state_jumps": "0.39% of consecutive same-pool trades (18,937 of 4.83M on train) show a >5% gap between one trade's computed post-state and the next trade's logged pre-state (297 of 2.13M >50% on Oct 1), not fixed by slot ordering; probably missed events or liquidity changes. Exits take the lower of the candidate states, so gaps count against the strategy."
 },
 "fill_model": "0.5 SOL, exact constant product on reserves (logged+17.585, logged tok), fee_bps/1e4 per side, entry at t+1 s at the HIGHER-priced of (state at t+1, post-state of first trade within 5 s after t+1); exit at the LOWER-priced of the analogous pair, and lower still if the next trade's pre-state is >2% lower. Tips 0.001 and 0.01 SOL per transaction, 2 per round trip.",
 "exploration": "Decile tables (train, 159,481 snapshots every 15 s in 689 active pools; and 59,886 in the 66 pools with SOL reserve >= 600) of OFI 60/180/300 s, returns 60/300 s, drawdown from post-migration high, distinct-wallet buy streak, distinct buyers 60 s, age, reserve, volume, largest 60 s sell and its recovery, vs 60/180/600 s net round trip: every decile had a negative mean before tips. High-OFI / many-buyer deciles in deep pools had positive medians and 70-84% win rates at 600 s but negative means (left tail of rug-like drops).",
 "n_configs_tested": 30,
